trip.js" defer></script><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/ui.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/theme.css"><script src="/assets/theme.js"></script><script src="/assets/search.js" defer></script><script src="/assets/live-news.js" defer></script><meta name="theme-color" content="#203f39"><link rel="icon" href="/assets/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="th" href="https://takuapa101.com/stories/apaporn/"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="en" href="https://takuapa101.com/en/stories/apaporn/"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="x-default" href="https://takuapa101.com/stories/apaporn/"></head><body class="inner-page"><a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a><header class="site-header"><a class="brand" href="/en/" aria-label="Takua Pa 101 Home"><span class="brand-mark">101</span><span>Takua Pa<small>TAKUA PA FIELD NOTES</small></span></a><nav id="main-nav" aria-label="Main menu"><a href="/en/places/">Places</a><a href="/en/stories/" aria-current="page">Stories</a><a href="/en/map/">Map</a><a href="/en/rest/">Eat and explore</a><a href="/en/news/">Updates</a><a href="/en/trip/">Your trip</a><a href="/en/traditions/" class="nav-more">Traditions</a><a href="/en/eat/" class="nav-more">Eat & Souvenirs</a><a href="/en/routes/" class="nav-more">Walking Routes</a><a href="/en/leaflet/" class="nav-more">Leaflet</a><a href="/en/about/" class="nav-more">About</a></nav><div class="header-tools"><a class="lang-switch" href="/stories/apaporn/" hreflang="th" lang="th">ไทย</a><button class="theme-toggle" type="button" data-theme-toggle aria-pressed="false" aria-label="Switch to dark mode"><span class="tt-night" aria-hidden="true">☾</span><span class="tt-day" aria-hidden="true">☀</span></button><button class="nav-toggle" type="button" data-nav-toggle aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="main-nav" aria-label="Open menu"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">☰</span></button><button class="icon-button" type="button" data-open-search aria-label="Search website (Press Ctrl+K)"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⌕</span></button><a class="icon-button" href="/en/trip/" aria-label="Your trip"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◫</span><span class="qs-badge" data-trip-count hidden>0</span></a><a class="header-map" href="/en/map/">Open map ↗</a></div></header><main id="main"><div class="story-article-v2"><header class="story-hero-v2"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/en/">Home</a><span>/</span><a href="/en/stories/">Takua Pa Stories</a><span>/</span><span>City topics</span></div><span class="eyebrow">Takua Pa Stories · Town Topics</span><h1>Aphon · The old town opens through clothing</h1><p class="lead">The first of the six A's in Takua Pa old town · Kebaya, patterns, and Peranakan beauty through Chang Pong's brush</p><p class="story-meta">ปรับปรุงเมื่อ 2026-09-09 · เวลาอ่าน 5 นาที</p></header><figure class="hero-photo-v2"><img src="/assets/photos/kuapapoh-charm-09.webp" width="900" height="1092" alt="Peranakan Charm No. 9 · A woman in a blue, gold-embroidered kebaya with a kosang brooch and gold bracelet, among peonies and butterflies." loading="eager"><figcaption><span>Peranakan Charm No. 9 · A woman in a blue, gold-embroidered kebaya with a kosang brooch and gold bracelet, among peonies and butterflies.</span><span class="credit">Changpong · Tinnapop Ngansathir</span></figcaption></figure><div class="story-layout-v2"><div class="story-main-v2"><div class="story-lede-v2"><p>The first of the six A's in Takua Pa old town is open · Aphon invites us to read the town through clothing, patterns, and accessories in Chang Pong's paintings.</p><p>Peranakan Charm is shown in September 2026 at 78 Studio on Takua Pa Culture Street. This story follows the project information and what is visible in the paintings; unverified history is marked clearly.</p></div><section class="story-section-v2"><h2 id="section-0">The six A's are a way to read the town</h2><figure class="section-photo-v2"><img src="/assets/culture-street.webp" width="1000" height="1000" alt="Takua Pa Old Town Cultural Street" loading="lazy"><figcaption><span>Takua Pa Old Town Cultural Street</span><span class="credit">Illustration</span></figcaption></figure><p>Kuapapoh presents six A's: Aphon, Asai, Ahan, Arom, Aram, and Akhan. They cover local clothing, ways of living, food, art and music, temples and shrines, and buildings and architecture.</p><p>Aphon opened first because the exhibition at 78 Studio gives us something to see immediately in September 2026 · clothing becomes the first doorway into the town's beauty and identity.</p></section><blockquote class="pull-quote-v2"><p>Peranakan Charm is evidence of identity across every stage of a life shaped by a love of art amid Peranakan culture.</p></blockquote><section class="story-section-v2"><h2 id="section-1">Peranakan clothing in the paintings</h2><figure class="section-photo-v2"><img src="/assets/photos/kuapapoh-charm-kebaya-pink.webp" width="900" height="1142" alt="A woman in a pink floral-embroidered kebaya, wearing three gold kosang brooches, against a blue background with roses." loading="lazy"><figcaption><span>A woman in a pink floral-embroidered kebaya, wearing three gold kosang brooches, against a blue background with roses.</span><span class="credit">Changpong · Tinnapop Ngansathir</span></figcaption></figure><p>The paintings show kebaya, a blue gold-embroidered kebaya, white cutwork lace, floral batik, kosang brooches, gold bracelets, and a lacquered tiffin carrier. These details appear together with color, flowers, backgrounds, and the women's poses.</p><p>The project describes Aphon as local clothing, lace, batik sarongs, textile patterns, and accessories. Chang Pong's paintings make that description visible.</p><p>The academic reason why a town shaped by mining has these clothes is not verified in the sources used here · what can be stated is that the project connects clothing with the town's story, while the artist conveys it through color, pattern, and dress.</p><div class="story-flags-v2"><span class="story-flag-v2 flag-unverified">The clothing's historical background is not verified</span></div></section><section class="story-section-v2"><h2 id="section-2">Peranakan Charm at 78 Studio</h2><figure class="section-photo-v2"><img src="/assets/photos/kuapapoh-expo-corner.webp" width="1400" height="1050" alt="The first corner of the exhibition at 78 Studio, with the artist biography on an easel and works hung on an old wooden shelf." loading="lazy"><figcaption><span>The first corner of the exhibition at 78 Studio, with the artist biography on an easel and works hung on an old wooden shelf.</span><span class="credit">Kuapapoh project · Ji Show Muang</span></figcaption></figure><p>The solo exhibition Peranakan Charm by Chang Pong · Tinnapop Ngansathin runs in September 2026 at 78 Studio on Takua Pa Culture Street. It uses brushwork to tell the town's story through pattern, color, and clothing, linking past and present.</p><p>โครงการกั่วป่าโพ้ฟื้นพื้นที่ว่างในอาคารเก่าให้เป็นพื้นที่สร้างสรรค์ บ้านเลขที่ 78 เดิมเป็นบ้านนายเหมืองและบริษัทเหมืองแร่ดีบุก ปัจจุบันเป็นกั่วป่าเหมืองมิวเซียมที่มีกิจกรรมหมุนเวียน · อ่านรายละเอียดของพื้นที่และโครงการได้ที่ <a href="https://kuapapoh.pages.dev/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">เว็บไซต์กั่วป่าโพ้</a></p><p>Chang Pong was born in Takua Pa old market. He studied at Silpakorn University, has exhibited his art, illustrated buildings and places in Phang Nga, worked on the film RAMBO 6, and makes book covers. He is now an assistant municipal artist and an independent artist.</p></section><section class="story-section-v2"><h2 id="section-3">Where to see it</h2><figure class="section-photo-v2"><img src="/assets/tao-ming.webp" width="1000" height="667" alt="Tao Ming School" loading="lazy"><figcaption><span>Tao Ming School</span><span class="credit">Illustration</span></figcaption></figure><p>Peranakan Charm is open every day at 78 Studio on Takua Pa Culture Street in September 2026. The project also lists house 109 as open Sundays and house 305 as open every Sunday.</p><p>ก่อนออกเดินทาง คุณตรวจสอบข่าวการจัดแสดงและรายละเอียดล่าสุดได้ที่ <a href="https://www.facebook.com/profile.php?id=61590430773715" target="_blank" rel="noopener">เพจกั่วป่าโพ้</a> และติดตามภาพรวมโครงการได้ที่ <a href="https://kuapapoh.pages.dev/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">กั่วป่าโพ้ · จีโชว์เมือง</a></p></section><section class="story-places-v2"><h2>Where to see it</h2><div class="mini-cards-v2"><div class="place-card-mini"><div><h3>Takua Pa Old Town Cultural Street</h3><button class="button button-outline" data-trip-add="culture-street">Add to trip</button></div></div><div class="place-card-mini"><div><h3>Tao Ming School</h3><button class="button button-outline" data-trip-add="tao-ming">Add to trip</button></div></div></div></section><details class="unknowns-box-v2"><summary>Missing data</summary><ul><li>The historical background of Peranakan clothing in Takua Pa</li><li>Official attendance and economic impact</li><li>The schedule after September 2026</li></ul></details><section class="story-sources-v2"><h2>Sources</h2><ol><li><cite>กั่วป่าโพ้ · ข้อมูลโครงการ</cite> · โครงการกั่วป่าโพ้ · content.json · hero, six, events, houses · <a href="https://kuapoh.pages.dev/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">View sources</a> (เข้าถึง 2026-09-09)</li><li><cite>เพจกั่วป่าโพ้</cite> · กั่วป่าโพ้ · หน้าสาธารณะของโครงการ · <a href="https://www.facebook.com/profile.php?id=61590430773715" target="_blank" rel="noopener">View sources</a> (เข้าถึง 2026-09-09)</li></ol></section></div><div class="story-sidebar-v2"><aside class="evidence-box-v2"><h3>Where is the evidence</h3><ul class="ev-items-v2"><li><div class="ev-claim">The six A's and the Aphon exhibition</div><div class="ev-status qualified">QUALIFIED</div><div class="ev-explain">Based on the project's published descriptions and schedule. <a href="https://kuapapoh.pages.dev/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">References ↗</a></div></li><li><div class="ev-claim">Clothing and accessories in the paintings</div><div class="ev-status qualified">QUALIFIED</div><div class="ev-explain">Described from the photo registry and project information only. <a href="https://kuapoh.pages.dev/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">References ↗</a></div></li><li><div class="ev-claim">The historical reason for this clothing in a mining town</div><div class="ev-status unverified">UNVERIFIED</div><div class="ev-explain">No confirming information appears in the sources used here. <a href="https://kuapoh.pages.dev/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">References ↗</a></div></li></ul></aside><nav class="story-toc-v2 scrollspy" id="story-toc"><h2>In this article</h2><ul class="scrollspy-nav"><li><a href="#section-0">The six A's are a way to read the town</a></li><li><a href="#section-1">Peranakan clothing in the paintings</a></li><li><a href="#section-2">Peranakan Charm at 78 Studio</a></li><li><a href="#section-3">Where to see it</a></li></ul></nav></div></div></div></main><footer class="site-footer"><div class="footer-top"><a href="/en/" class="footer-name">Takua Pa <em>101</em></a><p>One city<br>Stories to get to know</p><a class="round-link" href="#main" aria-label="Back to top">↑</a></div><div class="footer-bottom"><a href="https://siwaracafe.com/">Created by Baan Siwara, Takua Pa</a><span>Old Town Guide · Phang Nga Province</span><a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/pdf/travel-preview.pdf">Original Brochure ↗</a></div></footer><nav class="tabbar" aria-label="Quick menu"><a href="/en/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⌂</span>Home</a><a href="/en/map/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◈</span>Map</a><a href="/en/eat/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◉</span>Eat</a><a href="/en/trip/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◫</span>Trip<span class="qs-badge" data-trip-count hidden>0</span></a></nav></body></html>
